# relay persistence store
.hive-relay-data/

# Guardian's synced copy of the project
guardian-workspace/
.hive-mcp-session.json
# Per-client record of what THIS engine last wrote to each file — the cross-restart merge
# ancestor. Committing it would hand every clone a false ancestor for files it never wrote.
.hive-shadow.json
# Names a PID on this machine. Committed, it would tell every clone their folder is locked
# by a process that does not exist for them.
.hive-lock.json
# The Stop gate's watermark: how far through the room chat THIS machine's agent has been shown.
# Committed, a clone would inherit a position it never reached and go quiet about real mail.
.hive-stop-hook.json

.vercel
.env*

# ─── PRE-PUBLIC HYGIENE (2 Sep 2026) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Found by scanning the tree before considering a public repo. The git HISTORY is clean --
# 181 commits, zero real credentials -- so nothing here is a rewrite. These are all
# untracked files that a `git add -A` would publish.

# A LIVE API KEY is hardcoded in this file, twice. It has never been committed and must not
# be. The key itself should be rotated regardless: it has sat in plaintext on disk.
test_fireworks.py

# An entire third-party project, ~7,800 files, cloned into this repo. Publishing it would
# bury the ~50 files that are actually the product, and its own docs carry credential
# PLACEHOLDERS that read as leaks to every scanner.
hermes-agent/

